SUMMARY:Genomics and Microbiology Research Day
DESCRIPTION:This event is microscopic! The Genomics and Microbiology unit uses cutting-edge genomic technologies to explore the microscopic world of DNA inside a diversity of species from primates to planthopper insects\, and the microbes associated with them. We will highlight the research work going on here at the Museum and beyond. \n\nExhibits\nGenetics and Genomics Academy\nAt the Genetics and Genomics Academy\, we work with researchers within NC State and across North Carolina who are interested in genetics and genomics. We integrate genetics and genomic research\, education and outreach activities to forge a more interdisciplinary understanding of the genetic and genomic underpinnings of life on earth to sustain biodiversity and improve societal wellbeing. \nFermented Foods Microbes\nGenomics & Microbiology Research Lab\nExplore the microbes which help produce many of the tasty foods we love to enjoy and learn about some of the fermentation research in the Genomics & Microbiology Research Lab. \nFriend or Foe? Learn About the Microbes on Our Skin!\nGenomics & Microbiology Research Lab\nExplore the microbes on our skin and learn how researchers in the Genomics & Microbiology Research Lab use DNA to study them. \nWhat’s up with Monkey Blood?\nGenomics & Microbiology Research Lab\nLearn how you can participate in research with the Genomics & Microbiology Research Lab by participating in the Monkey Health Explorer project online and learn about monkey blood. \nWildlife CSI\nNC Wildlife Resources Commission\nBecome a wildlife crime scene investigator and learn about how the NCWRC uses genetics to combat illegal hunting and fishing to protect NC wildlife species and their habitats. \nGenetics Junction\nNC Wildlife Resources Commission\nUnleash your inner conservation geneticist and figure out what species live in the water by fishing for the DNA shed by animals into their environment. Will you find an elusive endangered species or uncover a pesky invasive? \nCheck Out the Lab!\nHead up to the 3rd floor to peek into the lab and learn what’s going on from Lab Head\, Dr. Liz Kierepka. Plus\, learn how we use genetic data to ID species that look VERY similar! \n\nPresentations- SECU Daily Planet Theater\n11 AM Microbes! The Hidden World On Us\nDr. Marianne Barrier\, Lab Manager\, Genomics & Microbiology Research Lab\, NC Museum of Natural Sciences\nLearn how researchers in the Genomics & Microbiology uses DNA to study the microscopic world living on our skin. \n12 PM From Rabid Raccoons to Recovering Rhinos: What Genomics Can Reveal About Wildlife\nDr. Liz Kierepka\, Lab Head\, Genomics & Microbiology Research Lab\, NC Museum of Natural Sciences\nLearn how genomics is a powerful tool to study wildlife in North Carolina and across the world.
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/genomics-research-day/
LOCATION:Downtown Raleigh\, 11 West Jones Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adults,All Ages,Educators,Special Events
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/NIK_7422.jpg
