UID:120894-1781605800-1781616600@www.naturalsciences.org
SUMMARY:Roots of Discovery: Juneteenth
DESCRIPTION:  \nStep into a celebration of freedom\, perseverance and creativity as we honor Juneteenth. Engage with the rich histories and cultural contributions of African American communities through interactive science\, storytelling and hands-on experiences. Trace the journey from past to present and discover how these legacies of resilience and innovation continue to shape our understanding of community\, inspire creativity and influence the world around us today. \nPresentation\n1:00pm\, SECU Daily Planet Theater\nCultivating Freedom\nExplore the powerful connection between agriculture\, liberation and resilience in Black communities through stories of land\, food and farming. Discover how these traditions continue to inspire community strength and sustainable change today. \nAbout the speaker\nKamal Bell is the founder of Sankofa Farms\, a regenerative farm and education hub based in Cedar Grove. As a Food Systems Architect\, Kamal uses agriculture as a tool to promote food access\, environmental stewardship\, youth education and stronger\, more resilient communities. \nActivities\nNature Research Center Lobby\nUV and Me\nNC Museum of Natural Sciences\nHumans all over the world have evolved various skin tones to adapt to varying levels of ultraviolet radiation from the sun. Learn how UV light illuminates a world that normally goes unseen to the unaided eye. \nSowing Seeds of Freedom\nNC African American Heritage Commission\nJoin the North Carolina African American Heritage Commission to learn about North Carolina’s Emancipation stories. Take home educational leaflets with planting instructions and the history behind seeds as symbols of freedom. \nAfrican American History & Genealogy Resources\nLibrary of North Carolina\nVisit the NC Government & Heritage Library to test your knowledge with NC Trivia and discover resources to support African American genealogy and historical research. \nBeginning Birding \nField Inclusive\nDiscover the sights\, sounds and other signs of common NC bird species\, as well as resources on how to create safer\, accessible and welcoming environments for birders of all backgrounds. \nJuneteenth with MOH \nNC Museum of History\nJuneteenth is a holiday that celebrates the freedom of people who had been enslaved. Learn about the Juneteenth flag and how it symbolizes freedom. And complete a puzzle to learn about the Thirteenth Amendment to the US Constitution. \n  \n\nRoots of Discovery series offers a meaningful platform where communities can share their stories in their own voice — through hands-on science\, artistic expression and cultural traditions — while showcasing the connections between culture\, nature and scientific discovery. \nJoin us for upcoming programs: \n\nNov 10 — Roots of Discovery: Festival of Light\n\n\n 
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/roots-of-discovery-juneteenth/
LOCATION:Downtown Raleigh\, 11 West Jones Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adults,All Ages,Children,General Events,SECU Daily Planet Theater,Teens
ORGANIZER;CN="Hugo%20Romero-Sanchez":MAILTO:hugo.romero@naturalsciences.org
GEO:35.7822735;-78.6395502
